1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,051
ATTORNEY WORKFLOW
Prepare a new civil case, submit the filing, and retain the receipt.

2
00:00:06,051 --> 00:00:11,284
01  |  YOUR FILING WORKSPACE
Start a new filing from the attorney dashboard.

3
00:00:11,284 --> 00:00:25,288
02  |  CHOOSE THE COURT
Select the court and start a new case.

4
00:00:25,288 --> 00:00:32,928
03  |  CASE TYPE & REQUIREMENTS
Choose Civil - General and review the documents needed for this demo filing.

5
00:00:32,928 --> 00:00:45,922
04  |  SAVE THE CASE DETAILS
Enter a fictional case title and description. Continuing saves the draft to the account.

6
00:00:45,922 --> 00:00:57,282
05  |  UPLOAD THE COMPLAINT
Select the document type, choose the sample PDF, and add it to the filing.

7
00:00:57,282 --> 00:01:11,147
06  |  ADD THE SUMMONS
Attach the summons to complete the documents required by this demo case type.

8
00:01:11,147 --> 00:01:17,915
07  |  REVIEW BEFORE SUBMITTING
Check the saved case details and the documents attached to the filing.

9
00:01:17,915 --> 00:01:27,528
08  |  SIMULATED PAYMENT
The $150 example fee is simulated. No card details are collected and no money is charged.

10
00:01:27,528 --> 00:01:33,847
09  |  SUBMIT THE FILING
Payment updates the review automatically. Submit the saved filing for court review.

11
00:01:33,847 --> 00:01:44,987
10  |  RETAIN THE SUBMISSION RECEIPT
The receipt records the filing and submission time. Court acceptance is a separate next step.
